<title>UK: Inchcape says buyers vie for Testing unit.</title>
<headline>Inchcape says buyers vie for Testing unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK-based distribution group Inchcape Plc said on Monday that there had been &quot;considerable interest&quot; in the sale of its Inchcape Testing Services unit, which it hoped to announce shortly.  </p>
<p>Inchcape reiterated that it expected to demerge its Bain Hogg insurance broker unit before the end of the year but gave no further details.</p>
<p>The company earlier posted flat first half pretax profits at 82.8 million stg and cut its half year dividend to 4.2 pence from 6.0 pence.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
